<title>BELGIUM: TABLE - EU's June inflation slightly up at 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - EU's June inflation slightly up at 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's annual inflation rate was 1.6 percent in June, up from 1.5 percent in May, but down from 2.4 percent a year ago, the EU statistics office Eurostat said.</p>
<p>Inflation was lowest in France and Austria with 1.0 percent each while Greece had the highest rate at 5.6 percent.</p>
<p>The rates are calculated as an average of member states' harmonised indices of consumer prices (HICPs).</p>
<p>Annual inflation measured by HICP</p>
<p>	  June 97   May 97   June 96</p>
<p>Belgium     1.6	1.5	1.9</p>
<p>Denmark     2.2	1.9	1.8</p>
<p>Germany     1.5	1.4	1.1</p>
<p>Greece	5.6	5.4	7.9</p>
<p>Spain	 1.4	1.3	3.6</p>
<p>France	1.0	0.9	2.5</p>
<p>Ireland     n/a	1.4	n/a</p>
<p>Italy	 1.6	1.7	3.9</p>
<p>Luxembourg  1.2	1.1	1.1</p>
<p>Netherlands 1.7	1.7	1.0</p>
<p>Austria     1.0	1.3	1.7</p>
<p>Portugal    1.6	1.9	3.4</p>
<p>Finland     1.1	0.9	1.1</p>
<p>Sweden	1.7	1.2	0.8</p>
<p>Britain     1.7	1.6	n/a</p>
<p>EU 15	 1.6	1.5	2.4</p>
<p>*n/a = not available</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
</text>
